# Artefact around or behind the entry modal: check the shadow first

A "box", light wedge or light line behind or around the entry modal was fixed
(confirmed by the user) in `_sheet_shadow` in `timesheet/ui/today.py`, not in
the widgets, the ghost windows or the scrim. Start there for similar reports.

What it was:

- The shadow shape is cast 2px downward. "Inside the dialog, skip it" was
  decided with the shifted shape, leaving an unshadowed strip under the
  dialog's bottom edge. Now the dialog's real outline decides, and the strip
  gets full shadow.
- Rows inside the dialog only looped over the side pads, so the four squares
  just outside the rounded corners were never shaded (light wedges). The corner
  columns are now included.

Checking it: read the shadow's own pixels (`surface._backdrop(x, y, 1, 1)`
against `_modal_backdrop`) at the corners and edges rather than capturing the
window. `PrintWindow` does not capture the canvas-drawn parts of the dialog.
